WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.644 --> 00:00:05.888
He stood as silent and white as the snow.

2
00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:09.250
His blue eyes were triangle-shaped.

3
00:00:10.331 --> 00:00:13.053
They were old tiles from a wall or floor.

4
00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.475
One eye hung close to his carrot nose.

5
00:00:17.596 --> 00:00:20.138
A large old comb had become his mouth.

6
00:00:21.259 --> 00:00:24.681
The uneven teeth made it appear as though he were frowning.

7
00:00:25.762 --> 00:00:28.584
Inside, however, the snowman was smiling.

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.301
He was alive.

9
00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:38.668
how cold it is today," the snowman exclaimed happily.

10
00:00:38.688 --> 00:00:43.853
"Woof! How can you be happy that it's cold?"

11
00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:45.214
barked Dog.

12
00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:48.897
Even Dog's fur could not keep him warm.

13
00:00:48.917 --> 00:00:51.399
"What do you mean?"

14
00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.741
Snowman was confused.

15
00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:56.584
"Everyone loves the cold winter.

16
00:00:57.504 --> 00:00:59.145
Just look at those children!"

17
00:01:00.145 --> 00:01:02.626
Three boys were having a snowball fight.

18
00:01:05.187 --> 00:01:07.868
Other children rode down a hill on sleds.

19
00:01:08.849 --> 00:01:10.550
They were all shouting with joy.

20
00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:15.352
"See? The cold makes everyone feel alive!"

21
00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:16.952
said Snowman.

22
00:01:16.972 --> 00:01:21.154
"Woof! Not everyone likes the cold."

23
00:01:22.435 --> 00:01:25.476
Dog lifted his head toward the shining sun.

24
00:01:28.836 --> 00:01:31.818
The sun's rays beamed down on the icy snow.

25
00:01:32.719 --> 00:01:36.221
Drops of water formed where the warm rays touched the snow.

26
00:01:36.241 --> 00:01:38.723
"What is that?"

27
00:01:39.323 --> 00:01:42.225
Snowman asked as he looked up at the sky.

28
00:01:43.106 --> 00:01:45.047
Snowman did not feel comfortable.

29
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:50.651
"It is called the sun," Dog answered.

30
00:01:51.932 --> 00:01:53.292
"See how it glows?

31
00:01:54.093 --> 00:01:56.334
It can melt away all this snow."

32
00:01:56.354 --> 00:02:02.658
"Melt? That sounds horrible," gasped Snowman.

33
00:02:02.678 --> 00:02:05.320
"I won't let it melt me."

34
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.001
Dog barked and barked.

35
00:02:08.441 --> 00:02:10.422
It sounded as though he were laughing.

36
00:02:10.442 --> 00:02:13.164
"We'll see about that!"

37
00:02:14.004 --> 00:02:15.245
Dog said nastily.

38
00:02:18.607 --> 00:02:22.489
Turning around three times, Dog went inside his doghouse.

39
00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:27.071
Snowman continued to watch the playful children.

40
00:02:29.204 --> 00:02:33.527
"I wish I could slide the way they do," he thought to himself.

41
00:02:34.568 --> 00:02:37.550
All day, Snowman stood still and silent.

42
00:02:38.451 --> 00:02:40.592
He did not dare look up at the sky.

43
00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:43.734
He knew Sun was there staring at him.

44
00:02:43.754 --> 00:02:48.818
"I won't let Sun get me," Snowman said firmly.

45
00:02:48.838 --> 00:02:51.099
"Children love the snow."

46
00:02:55.062 --> 00:02:57.884
Shortly after, something wonderful happened.

47
00:02:59.152 --> 00:03:00.893
Sun slowly disappeared.

48
00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:02.434
"I won!

49
00:03:03.154 --> 00:03:03.995
I won!"

50
00:03:04.715 --> 00:03:05.776
Snowman shouted.

51
00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:10.439
If he had had legs, Snowman would have jumped for joy.

52
00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:14.141
"Woof! What are you shouting for?"

53
00:03:15.381 --> 00:03:18.463
Dog came out of his house, yawning and stretching.

54
00:03:18.483 --> 00:03:21.805
"Look! Sun has gone away.

55
00:03:21.825 --> 00:03:24.727
And it didn't melt me!"

56
00:03:25.387 --> 00:03:26.428
Snowman cried.

57
00:03:29.488 --> 00:03:33.131
If he had had arms, Snowman would have waved to the sky.

58
00:03:34.211 --> 00:03:36.393
Again Dog laughed and laughed.

59
00:03:37.674 --> 00:03:40.776
"Sun will be back tomorrow.

60
00:03:41.036 --> 00:03:43.338
But now Moon, his friend, is here."

61
00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:47.381
Dog looked up at the dark sky and howled.

62
00:03:48.381 --> 00:03:50.102
Snowman carefully looked up.

63
00:03:51.243 --> 00:03:54.666
Indeed, a white round ball had replaced Sun.

64
00:03:54.686 --> 00:03:57.708
"Can Moon melt snow too?"

65
00:03:58.564 --> 00:03:59.324
asked Snowman.

66
00:03:59.344 --> 00:04:04.086
"Of course not," barked Dog.

67
00:04:04.106 --> 00:04:06.786
"But Moon keeps shining.

68
00:04:07.366 --> 00:04:10.167
So tomorrow Sun will know where you are."

69
00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.588
Snowman felt afraid.

70
00:04:13.108 --> 00:04:14.088
He looked around.

71
00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.709
The children were all gone too.

72
00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:20.950
"I'm all alone," he said sadly.

73
00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:24.691
"Well, too bad," barked Dog.

74
00:04:25.471 --> 00:04:28.212
"I would stay but it's time for my dinner."

75
00:04:29.212 --> 00:04:31.073
Dog trotted toward the house.

76
00:04:32.014 --> 00:04:34.075
He barked and scratched at the door.

77
00:04:36.157 --> 00:04:39.339
A young boy opened it and Dog disappeared inside.

78
00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:43.262
All night, Snowman stood still and silent.

79
00:04:44.182 --> 00:04:48.585
Early the next morning, just as Dog had said, Sun was back.

80
00:04:49.726 --> 00:04:53.048
"So you have returned," Snowman said to Sun.

81
00:04:53.068 --> 00:04:56.671
"Well, you won't melt me today, either!"

82
00:04:57.251 --> 00:04:58.332
Snowman shouted.

83
00:05:00.644 --> 00:05:03.625
Snowman watched as children came out to play again.

84
00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:06.086
Some stopped to look at him.

85
00:05:06.106 --> 00:05:11.907
"His eye is falling," a little girl said.

86
00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.828
She pulled the hanging tile off.

87
00:05:15.688 --> 00:05:17.809
Then she shoved it next to the other one.

88
00:05:17.829 --> 00:05:20.209
"Thank you.

89
00:05:20.689 --> 00:05:24.250
Now I can see much better," Snowman thought.

90
00:05:25.231 --> 00:05:26.831
Snowman was very happy.

91
00:05:26.851 --> 00:05:31.505
"Little children must like me," he said to himself.

92
00:05:31.525 --> 00:05:34.407
"They come up to me and smile."

93
00:05:34.427 --> 00:05:39.251
"Excuse me," a small voice called from below.

94
00:05:41.412 --> 00:05:42.633
Snowman looked down.

95
00:05:43.253 --> 00:05:44.734
It was a little rabbit.

96
00:05:44.754 --> 00:05:49.338
"Yes?" Snowman said.

97
00:05:49.358 --> 00:05:53.621
"It's very cold," began Rabbit.

98
00:05:53.641 --> 00:05:57.864
"It is indeed," Snowman said happily.

99
00:05:59.152 --> 00:06:01.153
"I can't find any food to eat.

100
00:06:02.393 --> 00:06:06.975
I just wish this horrible winter would end," cried Rabbit.

101
00:06:07.956 --> 00:06:10.477
Suddenly, he saw Snowman's nose.

102
00:06:10.497 --> 00:06:15.979
"My, what a fine nose you have," said Rabbit.

103
00:06:16.499 --> 00:06:17.579
He licked his lips.

104
00:06:21.081 --> 00:06:23.382
Snowman looked down at his carrot nose.

105
00:06:24.562 --> 00:06:25.883
Then he looked at Rabbit.

106
00:06:26.823 --> 00:06:28.604
Rabbit did look cold and thin.

107
00:06:29.712 --> 00:06:31.413
"Do you want my nose?"

108
00:06:32.093 --> 00:06:32.994
Snowman asked.

109
00:06:33.014 --> 00:06:35.895
"Oh, would you mind?"

110
00:06:36.816 --> 00:06:38.017
Rabbit asked eagerly.

111
00:06:38.037 --> 00:06:43.159
"Not at all," Snowman said kindly.

112
00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.041
Rabbit plucked the carrot off.

113
00:06:46.061 --> 00:06:48.522
"Thank you so much!"

114
00:06:49.423 --> 00:06:51.224
Rabbit waved and hopped away.

115
00:06:52.344 --> 00:06:54.565
So once again, Snowman was alone.

116
00:06:57.867 --> 00:06:59.288
Sun stayed out all day.

117
00:06:59.856 --> 00:07:01.757
But he could not melt Snowman.

118
00:07:02.877 --> 00:07:04.317
Then Moon came out again.

119
00:07:04.337 --> 00:07:08.118
"I'm still here!"

120
00:07:08.759 --> 00:07:09.699
laughed Snowman.

121
00:07:09.719 --> 00:07:13.100
"Your friend Sun couldn't melt me!"

122
00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:17.881
Moon remained silent but he kept his light on Snowman.

123
00:07:18.921 --> 00:07:23.303
Day and night, Sun and Moon took turns shining down on Snowman.

124
00:07:24.323 --> 00:07:27.864
Day and night, Snowman tried to keep standing straight.

125
00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.741
Then one day, something happened.

126
00:07:34.422 --> 00:07:38.904
"I don't feel so good," Snowman said to Dog.

127
00:07:39.965 --> 00:07:42.466
Dog had not gone into the house that night.

128
00:07:42.967 --> 00:07:44.768
He stayed in his house outside.

129
00:07:44.788 --> 00:07:49.790
"That's because the weather is changing," barked Dog.

130
00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:53.172
"Changing? But why?

131
00:07:53.832 --> 00:07:56.874
Everyone loves winter," Snowman cried.

132
00:07:56.894 --> 00:08:02.877
"Maybe," said Dog, "but everyone loves spring too."

133
00:08:08.239 --> 00:08:09.140
What is that?"

134
00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:10.820
Snowman asked.

135
00:08:12.221 --> 00:08:15.762
"Spring is the time for flowers and trees to blossom.

136
00:08:16.603 --> 00:08:19.744
Grass grows back," explained Dog.

137
00:08:19.764 --> 00:08:22.585
"But what about the snow?

138
00:08:23.225 --> 00:08:24.206
What about me?"

139
00:08:25.026 --> 00:08:26.487
Snowman asked quietly.

140
00:08:27.647 --> 00:08:29.148
Dog laughed and laughed.

141
00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.562
"I told you!

142
00:08:32.962 --> 00:08:34.763
Sun will melt you away."

143
00:08:35.964 --> 00:08:37.224
Snowman looked down.

144
00:08:38.025 --> 00:08:40.566
There was a growing puddle around his body.

145
00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:45.949
"But don't worry," barked Dog.

146
00:08:45.969 --> 00:08:48.331
"You'll be back next winter."

147
00:08:48.351 --> 00:08:50.392
"I will?"

148
00:08:51.172 --> 00:08:51.973
asked Snowman.

149
00:08:51.993 --> 00:08:57.096
"Yes, you come back every winter," said Dog.

150
00:08:58.512 --> 00:09:00.593
Snowman thought about Dog's words.

151
00:09:00.613 --> 00:09:03.655
"Will I see you next winter?"

152
00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:04.936
he asked.

153
00:09:07.598 --> 00:09:09.519
Dog turned around three times.

154
00:09:13.301 --> 00:09:17.104
course!" he barked and went inside his house.

155
00:09:18.204 --> 00:09:21.006
"Good-bye, friend," Snowman called out.

156
00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:24.068
Then he slowly disappeared.
